# Upstream starter-template baseline for the predefined workspace files.
#
# Each line is the first 32 characters of the sha256 of one OpenClaw starter
# template, taken from the version recorded below, after stripping its YAML
# front matter — which is how the gateway itself loads a template. The files in
# workspace-templates/ were derived from exactly these bodies and then
# customized, so they cannot be compared to upstream directly: they are meant
# to differ.
#
# scripts/check-forward-compat.sh compares a newer release's templates against
# these digests, so the only thing it reports is upstream changing out from
# under the predefined copies. Refresh this file in the same commit that raises
# ARG OPENCLAW_VERSION, after reviewing what changed.
#
# The digests are truncated to 32 hex characters on purpose. A full 64-character
# digest is an unbroken run of [A-Za-z0-9], which scripts/check-secrets.sh
# rightly treats as possible base64 and reports as a leaked token. 128 bits is
# far more than enough to notice a template edit, so truncating here keeps that
# scanner strict rather than carving out an exception for this file.
#
# This lives in scripts/ rather than workspace-templates/ because
# docker/entrypoint.sh seeds that directory with "cp -rn <dir>/." which copies
# hidden files too, so anything placed there lands in every agent workspace.
#
# derived-from: openclaw@2026.10.7

490fc2b32865dd310a3af1225a409ac5  AGENTS.md
f1ca0312afae15dee389671c566cb25c  SOUL.md
d1b9cea71ba4214fdd266b2b2a28adca  IDENTITY.md
46e0d8c937df7b104de97a23c5853729  USER.md
